T-02 - C18 IMPLEMENTED AS CODE
------------------------------
Was prompt-bullet text at script line ~901 only; never executed. Now def c18().

Why it does not guess: authority_filings entries carry NO field naming the spec
that realises them, and filing_id does not track spec filenames -
  BE-FIN-BV-003   is realised by BE-FIN-001-Finprof274-Spec.xlsx
  BE-NSSO-ASR-006 is realised by BE-NSSO-004-DRS-Spec.xlsx
                  (ASR and DRS are the Dutch and French names of one declaration)
Heuristics were prototyped and MEASURED on BE and produce confident WRONG
matches (token "NSSO" matches all 5 NSSO specs; "003" matches DmfAModification;
"FIN" matches FEBELFIN). An audit check that guesses is worse than one that
abstains, so C18 splits into sub-rules that cannot be wrong:

  C18.1 in_scope non-empty but zero Spec files on disk            -> FAIL
  C18.2 a filing DECLARES a spec_file and the file is absent      -> FAIL
  C18.3 a Spec matches only out_of_scope filings AND does not
        declare itself descoped                                   -> FAIL
  C18.4 filing_id duplicated, or in both scope lists              -> FAIL
  C18.5 a filing declares no spec link at all                     -> MANUAL,
        listing unverified candidates so a human closes it cheaply

Token discrimination is data-driven, not a hardcoded per-country stop-list: a
token matching >=3 spec filenames is an authority/agency label and is dropped;
one matching 1-2 is kept (two is the normal shape of an obligation plus its
correction channel, e.g. DmfA + DmfAModification).

Accepted link fields: spec_file, spec_files, report_spec, report_specs, spec,
realized_by. Populating spec_file on each in_scope entry converts every C18.5
into C18.2 and makes C18 fully deterministic - that is the recommended follow-up.

